= [Strand equivariance]
- Hypothesis: during training, models see the same sequence twice, once in the original direction and once reverse complemented. What is the difference between predictions for the original and reverse complemented sequence?

= [Does adding DNA sequences from human DNA improve performance and why not?]
- Hypothesis: Yorzoi is trained on roughly 10 Mb of human DNA. This includes novel terminator and promoter motifs. Yet, adding all this data doesn't result in performance improvements on any benchmark task that we developed. 